# XSH fputws()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.fputws.001
anchor     functions/fputws.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputws.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/fputws.html#APPLICATION USAGE
class      required
says       fputws(L"hi") on a stream opened "w" returns a non-negative value,
           ftell() is then 2, and after fclose() the file holds exactly "hi": no
           null character and no newline.
test       t/001-writes.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.002
anchor     functions/fputws.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputws.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       fputws(L"") returns a non-negative value and writes nothing;
           fputws(L"a") and fputws(L"b") then leave the file holding "ab".
test       t/002-empty.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.003
anchor     functions/fputws.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.5
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, fputws() of a string made of the wide character
           mbrtowc() gives for 0xc3 0xa9 followed by L'x' returns a non-negative
           value and the file then holds the bytes 0xc3 0xa9 'x'.
test       t/003-multibyte.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.004
anchor     functions/fputws.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputwc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
anchor     functions/fputws.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       On a stream opened "w" whose descriptor was closed (unbuffered where
           allowed, otherwise written until the buffer needs flushing), the
           failing fputws() returns -1, sets errno to EBADF and sets the error
           indicator.
test       t/004-ebadf-closed.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.005
anchor     functions/fputws.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputwc.html#ERRORS/EPIPE
anchor     functions/fputws.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With SIGPIPE blocked, on a stream on the write end of a pipe whose
           read end is closed, the failing fputws() returns -1, sets errno to
           EPIPE and sets the error indicator.
test       t/005-epipe.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.006
anchor     functions/fputws.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputwc.html#ERRORS/EILSEQ
anchor     functions/fputws.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       In a UTF-8 locale, fputws() of L"a", a wide-character code that
           wcrtomb() rejects, and L"b" returns -1, sets errno to EILSEQ and sets
           the error indicator.
test       t/006-eilseq.c

assertion  XSH.fputws.007
anchor     functions/fputws.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       After the modification time of a file is set to 2001-09-09, fputws()
           on a stream opened "r+" on it followed by fflush() leaves the
           modification time later.
test       t/007-mtime.c
